From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ClayWarren <warren.clay@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/link: use external linking for unsupported ARM64 COFF

The ARM64 internal PE loader cannot select associative COMDAT children or
process ARM64 exception-handling data. Inspect host objects before choosing
link mode so ordinary cgo builds use the external linker when needed,
without partially loading these sections or dropping unwind information.

Keep supported leaf and resource inputs eligible for internal linking and
leave other architectures unchanged. Bound reads to the archive member,
preserve its reader state, and let the external linker validate COFF forms
that debug/pe cannot parse. Explicit external linking remains opaque;
explicit internal linking and late-only unsupported archive members fail
with a causal diagnostic instead of partially creating loader state.

Tests cover COMDAT strategies, initialized and BSS static data leaders,
long section names, invalid section definitions, packed/full/ordered unwind,
empty sections, resources, AMD64, archive offsets, short inputs, automatic
selection, and explicit internal-link rejection through flag and environment.

---
